{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "2: Set up Auth0 and run Z-Assistant",
  "nextTour": "3: Add Standard Tools",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "About Z-Assistant",
      "description": "## About Z-Assistant\n\nZ-Assistant is a Node.js Express application. This Codespace has already installed all required dependencies, including:\n\n- [express-openid-connect](https://github.com/auth0/express-openid-connect) — Auth0 OIDC middleware for user authentication\n- [Vercel AI SDK](https://sdk.vercel.ai) — Tool calling and streaming for the AI agent\n- [@auth0/ai-vercel](https://auth0.com/ai/docs/sdks/vercel-ai-sdk) — Auth0 AI integrations including CIBA\n\nThe lab also includes **RetailZero API** — a local mock e-commerce API running on port 3001 that Z-Assistant will call using its tools."
    },
    {
      "title": "Understanding the code",
      "description": "## Understanding the code\n\nHere is the project structure:\n\n```\nz-assistant/src/\n├── app.ts               # Express server — OIDC, SSE chat endpoint\n├── lib/\n│   ├── auth0.ts         # AsyncLocalStorage + getUserID() helper\n│   └── auth0-ai.ts      # You will add CIBA wrappers here (Tour 5)\n├── tools/\n│   └── retailzero.ts    # Vercel AI SDK tool definitions for the RetailZero API\n└── public/\n    ├── index.html       # Z-Assistant chat UI\n    └── app.js           # SSE stream reader, CIBA retry logic\n\nretailzero-api/src/\n├── app.ts               # RetailZero mock API server (port 3001)\n└── data/\n    ├── products.ts      # Product catalog\n    ├── orders.ts        # Order data\n    └── customers.ts     # Customer profiles (public + private PII)\n```"
    },
    {
      "file": "z-assistant/.env.local",
      "description": "## Generate an application secret\n\nZ-Assistant uses a secret to sign encrypted session cookies. Let's generate one.\n\n1. [Select this link](command:codetour.sendTextToTerminal?[\"openssl rand -hex 32\"]) to run `openssl rand -hex 32` in the terminal.\n2. Copy the output and paste it as the value for `AUTH0_SECRET` on the highlighted line above.",
      "line": 2,
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 2,
          "character": 15
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 2,
          "character": 70
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Set the APP_BASE_URL",
      "file": "z-assistant/.env.local",
      "description": "## Set the APP_BASE_URL\n\nZ-Assistant needs to know its public URL for Auth0 redirects.\n\n1. [Select this link](command:codetour.sendTextToTerminal?[\"echo https://$CODESPACE_NAME-3000.app.github.dev\"]) to print your Codespace app URL to the terminal. It should look something like: `https://xxxxx-xxxxx-xxxxx-3000.app.github.dev`\n2. Copy the output and set it as the value for `APP_BASE_URL`.\n\nIt should look something like like: `https://xxxxx-xxxxx-xxxxx-3000.app.github.dev`\n",
      "line": 3,
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 1,
          "character": 12
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 1,
          "character": 24
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Create an Auth0 application",
      "description": "## Create an Auth0 application\n\n1. From the Auth0 Dashboard, go to **Applications** > **Applications**.\n\n1. Create a new application with the following details:\n   - **Name**: Z-Assistant\n   - **Application type**: Regular Web Application\n\n2. On the application's **Settings** tab, scroll to **Application URIs** and configure these fields as specified:\n   - **Allowed Callback URLs**: [select this link](command:codetour.sendTextToTerminal?[\"echo \\\"https://$CODESPACE_NAME-3000.app.github.dev/auth/callback\\\"\"]) and copy/paste the terminal output (This will look like: `https://xxxxx-xxxxx-xxxxx-3000.app.github.dev/auth/callback`).\n   - **Allowed Logout URLs**: [select this link](command:codetour.sendTextToTerminal?[\"echo \\\"https://$CODESPACE_NAME-3000.app.github.dev/\\\"\"]) and copy/paste the terminal output (this will look like: `https://xxxxx-xxxxx-xxxxx-3000.app.github.dev/`).\n\n3. **Save** these changes."
    },
    {
      "file": "z-assistant/.env.local",
      "description": "## Set AUTH0_DOMAIN\n\n1. On your Auth0 application's **Settings** tab, find the **Domain** field in Basic Information.\n2. Copy the domain value (e.g. `dev-abc123.us.auth0.com`) and paste it on the highlighted line above.\n\n    > Note: Do **not** add `https://` to this. Just copy and paste the domain as-is.",
      "line": 4,
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 4,
          "character": 15
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 4,
          "character": 27
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "file": "z-assistant/.env.local",
      "description": "## Set AUTH0_CLIENT_ID\n\n1. From the same **Settings** tab, copy the **Client ID**.\n2. Paste it as the value for `AUTH0_CLIENT_ID` on the highlighted line above.",
      "line": 5,
      "selection": {
