    {
      "title": "Start the RetailZero API",
      "description": "## Start the RetailZero API\n\nZ-Assistant's tools call the **RetailZero API** which runs separately on port 3001.\n\n1. [Select this link](command:workbench.action.terminal.new) to open a new terminal tab.\n2. [Select this link](command:codetour.sendTextToTerminal?[\"cd retailzero-api && npm run dev\"]) to start the RetailZero API.\n>When the dialog appears, select Open in Browser to open the app.\n>Alternatively, go to the PORTS tab and select the globe icon next to port 3001.\n\nIn the terminal, you should see:\n```\nRetailZero API running at http://localhost:3001\n```\n\n> Keep this terminal open — the API must stay running throughout the lab."
    },
    {
      "title": "Test Z-Assistant",
      "description": "## Test Z-Assistant\n\nNow let's run Z-Assistant and verify the Auth0 integration works.\n\n1. [Start Z-Assistant](command:workbench.action.debug.start).\n2. When the dialog appears, select **Open in Browser** to open the app.\n   > Alternatively, go to the **PORTS** tab and select the globe icon next to port 3000.\n3. Log in to the application.\n4. Ask Z-Assistant something simple: _\"What can you help me with?\"_\n\nYou should get a response describing Z-Assistant's capabilities. Since we haven't added tools yet, it can only reply from its training knowledge — not from live RetailZero data.\n\n5. [Stop the application](command:workbench.action.debug.stop) when done.\n\nIn the next tour we will add the RetailZero tools."
    }
  ]
}